<title>CANADA: Cambior halts Gonzague-Langlois output.</title>
<headline>Cambior halts Gonzague-Langlois output.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cambior Inc said on Tuesday that it temporarily halted zinc production at its Gonzague-Langlois mine in Lebel-sur-Quevillon, Quebec to modify mining methods and because of weakness in the zinc market.</p>
<p>About 100 employees will be laid off temporarily, the company said. A new mining plan has been established and certain workers will be assigned to underground development work and the preparation of new stopes.</p>
<p>Cambior said it expects to restart production in the second quarter of 1997 in more favourable zinc market conditions.</p>
<p>(Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434)</p>
